                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure D.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Extract from translation of income-tax law of Japan,
                        as published by the Yokohama tax bureau.</hi></head>
                <p>Art. V. Income tax is not levied on the following incomes:</p>
                <p>1. Salaries of persons in the army or navy while on active service.</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Extract from treaty between the
                        United States and Japan, signed November 22, 1894.</hi></p>
                <p>Art. 1, par. 4. They (the subjects or citizens of each of the two high
                    contracting parties) shall not be compelled, under any pretext whatever, to pay
                    any charges or taxes other or higher than those that are, or may be, paid by
                    native subjects or citizens or subjects or citizens of the most favored
                    nation.</p>
            </div>
